# Playing the first release, from orbit to a working territory.
#
# `releases/first-release.md` gives the loop. This file walks the first four steps of it:
# no presence on the planet, land the ark and found a territory, build structures manned
# by the population, and build infrastructure to mine metal and energy.
#
# Every line is a command. There is no other way for the state to move, so this file is a
# complete account of the game it produces.

# 1 and 2: the ark comes down and founds the landing site.
land ark 1

# Ending the turn is what transforms it: the ark is consumed and becomes a garrison to
# hold the ground, one citizen, and an extractor working a food node.
end turn

# Turn 2. One citizen, so one unit of labor. It works the food node.
work 1 extractor 1 food
end turn

# Turn 3. Two citizens. One builds a second farm, the other works the first.
build extractor 1 food
work 1 extractor 1 food
end turn

# Turn 4. Four citizens, and the third food node is taken. Every farm is worked.
build extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 food
end turn

# Turn 5. Eight citizens. Food first, then the metal nodes are opened.
work 3 extractor 1 food
build extractor 1 metal
build extractor 1 metal
build extractor 1 metal
work 2 extractor 1 metal
end turn

# Turn 6. Twelve citizens, which is every hand the food here can feed. All three
# resources are worked, and the territory is at its ceiling: twelve of each per turn.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
build extractor 1 energy
build extractor 1 energy
build extractor 1 energy
work 3 extractor 1 energy

# Still turn 6. Twelve metal and twelve energy are on the ground, and a
# Pioneer costs eight and six - so the landing site can now send one out. This is step 5
# of the loop: spread across the planet by land.
produce pioneer 1
end turn

# Turn 7. The farms are worked first: a population that gathers nothing this turn starves
# at the end of it, whatever else is going on elsewhere.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 3 extractor 1 energy

# Then the pioneer crosses into a neighbouring territory. It is not controlled, so
# moving there takes it: force 2 against a force of nature of 1.
move pioneer 2

# Ending the turn transforms it, exactly as the ark was transformed - a garrison to hold
# the new ground, a citizen, and an extractor on its best food node.
end turn
